  "published": "2026-04-24T20:05:22.187Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.4 patch: Fixes browser-side `IRTCRtpSender.SetParameters` which threw `TypeError: Failed to read the 'codecs' property from 'RTCRtpParameters': Required member is undefined` on every call in 1.1.3. Root cause: our cross-platform DTO -> BlazorJS native translation dropped `codecs` / `headerExtensions` / `rtcp` (which are required-present per W3C spec even when read-only). Fix: cache the native `getParameters` object per-sender and mutate only the mutable fields on `setParameters`, preserving the required-present fields. 2 browser simulcast tests that were failing on 1.1.3 now pass. Desktop path unchanged. Consumers of SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.3 via SpawnDev.WebTorrent 3.1.3 pick up the fix on next `dotnet restore` via the >= 1.1.3 transitive pin; no WebTorrent bump required unless consumers lock-file the exact 1.1.3 version.",
